  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through Tuesday)\nIssued at 938 PM CDT Tue Oct 13 2026\n\nA fast-moving upper trough will swing through the Ohio/Tennessee \nValleys on Friday and pivot into the Southern Appalachians Friday \nnight into early Saturday. Very breezy conditions will accompany \nthis feature, with a strong push of cool, dry air moving into the \nregion in its wake. This can be seen with temperatures as they \nwill drop off significantly Friday night, eventually settling into\nthe mid to upper 40s in most locations by early Saturday morning.\nBreezy post frontal winds out of the NNE will reinforce this air \nmass as highs will be very notably lower on Saturday and only peak\nin the mid to upper 60s, and lows again dropping to the 40s. \nWinds will weaken by Sunday and veer to a more southerly direction\nas high pressure builds in. This will do little to modify the air\nmass initially as highs on Sunday will only peak in the mid/upper\n60s to lower 70s. Ridging really begins to take shape on Monday \nand Tuesday of next week, resulting in a gradual warming trend, \nthanks to ample sunshine and southerly flow. Daytime highs in the \nmid to upper 70s will be common, with lows in the low to mid 50s.",
